= University of California San Diego School of Medicine - Prompt 01

#section_label("Prompt metadata")
- Title: Autobiographical Statement
- Limit: 6000 characters
- Cycle used in this repo: 2024 archive on Admit.org
- Source: https://med.admit.org/secondary-essays/university-of-california-san-diego-school-of-medicine
- Local notes file: prompt-01.local.md

#section_label("Prompt text")
This should be a true autobiographical statement. Topics to be included are family, childhood, primary and secondary school years, undergraduate years, and, if applicable, what you’ve done since completing your bachelor’s degree. You should also discuss the motivational factors which led you to a career in medicine, including any disadvantages or obstacles which might put your accomplishments into context.

#section_label("Shared backbone files")
- typst/shared/challenge.typ
- typst/shared/future-goals.typ

#section_label("challenge backbone")
= Challenge / Adversity Backbone

== Situation
Describe the challenge clearly and briefly.

== Response
- What did you do?
- What tradeoffs or hard decisions did you make?
- Who did you rely on?

== Growth
- What changed in you?
- How will this matter in medicine?
#section_label("future-goals backbone")
= Future Goals Backbone

== Near-Term
What do you hope to learn or become in medical school?

== Longer-Term
What kind of physician or leader are you building toward?

== Continuity
Connect your future goals to real prior experiences.

